# Core pipeline

- Functions here are pure: data in, data out. No `fetch`, files, `Date.now()`, `process.env` or Telegram. Pass the logger in when warnings are needed (`normalize(results, log)`).
- Compare and subtract money in kopecks via `toKopecks` from `money.js`; convert to UAH only for display.

```js
// ❌ 56.99 - 56.69 === 0.30000000000000426
const delta = price - previous;
// ✅
const delta = (toKopecks(price) - toKopecks(previous)) / 100;
```

- Fuel codes, their post order and labels live only in `fuels.js` (`FUEL_CODES`, `FUEL_LABELS`). Do not hardcode codes elsewhere.
- `FUEL_MAP` keys must match the site byte for byte; watch Cyrillic/Latin look-alikes (`А`/`A`, `Е`/`E`). A `null` value means "known, deliberately skipped" (AdBlue); a missing key means "unknown, warn".
- A suspicious price is dropped and reported through `rejected`, never corrected or rounded into plausibility.
- Every behavior change needs a test in `test/<module>.test.js`; the scenarios to cover are listed in `docs/development.md` and `docs/storage-and-comparison.md`.
